><name>SUGIYAMA OSAMU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>CITIZEN WATCH CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KASAI, HIDEFUMI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIYA, YUKIO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUGIYAMA, OSAMU</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KASAI HIDEFUMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MIYA YUKIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUGIYAMA OSAMU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KASAI, HIDEFUMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIYA, YUKIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUGIYAMA, OSAMU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A diamond-like carbon film (30) is formed on that part, at least in contact with a stamper (6), of the surface (2a) of a movable mold (2) to which the stamper (6) is attached and which, together with a fixed mold (1), forms a cavity (5) of a resin molding mold, via an intermediate layer (20) consisting of silicon, tungsten, titanium carbide, silicon carbide, chromium carbide and the like for increasing an adhesion power with respect to the surface (2a) of the mold (2), thereby dramatically prolonging a service life of a resin molding mold and a lifetime of a stamper without damaging it.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur un film (30) diamantoïde formé sur une partie, en contact avec un dispositif d'estampage (6), de la surface (2a) d'un moule (2) amovible auquel est relié le dispositif d'estampage (6), et qui, avec un moule fixe (1), forme une cavité (5) de moule pour moulage de résine, au moyen d'une couche intermédiaire (20) constituée de silicium, tungstène, carbure de titane, carbure de silicium, carbure de chrome et autre de façon à accroître la force d'adhésion par rapport à la surface (2a) du moule (2), ce qui prolonge énormément la durée de vie utile estimative d'un moule pour moulage de résine et la durée de vie d'un dispositif d'estampage sans l'endommager.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>